From e79e54580e7071cec3632c5d1913a32daf4b2974 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:19:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] wayland: Optionally show the running scene and the result on
 screen

With --winsys-options wayland-overlay=true, a small bar at the bottom
shows the running scene with its frame rate, frame time and position,
updated twice a second, and at the end a card shows the score with the
frame rate of every scene until a tap, a click or a key. Useful where
vkmark is started without a terminal, e.g. from a launcher on a phone.

The overlay is a desynchronized sub-surface with shm buffers drawn by
cairo, so the compositor blends it and the scenes' GPU work stays the
same. It follows the window's scale (wp_viewporter or buffer scale).
Without cairo the option has no effect.

The window system gets show_status() and show_result(), which do
nothing by default; MainLoop counts the scenes and keeps each scene's
result.
